# A humor bends a crafting roll
#
# Every thing made at a station is rolled in the dice box, like any other roll, and the viscera's humors
# may bend its dice before the result is accepted. Here a forced miss leaves the nail's dice without a
# six; the hepar's spendable humor is blood (+1 to a die), spent on a five, and the six it makes turns the
# spoiled nail into a made one. The blood is gone from the hepar afterwards (the queue moves up one).
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --grant-mm blacksmithing,bladesmithing --grant-item hammer,smith_tongs,horseshoe --organs hands=2 --location-type test --location-id 0 --start-area "Test Ruin" --period dawn --observe-only "Test Old Anvil"

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

strategy succeed
goal use
means blacksmithing
advance 12 180
click keyword 0
choose 0
choose ripelore
advance 12 180
click action 0
choose 1
choose 0
advance 12 180
click action 1
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180
click button
wait mode Crafting 30

craft break horseshoe
expect-state crafting pool=2

strategy fail-dice
craft make nail
wait
expect-state crafting rolling item=nail dice=13 needed=1 sixes=0 settled=yes would=spoil humors=yes
expect-state humors hepar Yellow Bile=23 Phlegm=11 Blood=10

# Blood on the five: the die becomes a six and the roll succeeds.
click humor hepar
click die 1
wait
expect-state crafting sixes=1 settled=yes would=make humors=yes
expect-state humors hepar Yellow Bile=23 Phlegm=12 Blood=9

craft settle
expect-state crafting result=made
expect-state crafting pool=1
expect-state items nail
craft leave
wait mode LocationInteraction 30
save roundtrip
quit
